 "hook": "800 MILES OF LINES",
 "description": "The Nazca lines are geoglyphs in the soil of the Nazca Desert in southern Peru, made between 500 BC and 500 AD by removing reddish-brown pebbles to expose lighter subsoil. Their combined length is more than 1,300 km, and drones have found several hundred new figures this century. Imagery: Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics. Photos: Diego Delso, CC BY-SA 4.0, Wikimedia Commons. Source: Wikipedia.",
